# PackageManager: always extract native libraries of apps that are not on the system image (WSA).
#
# An ARM-only app installed on this x86_64 device with extractNativeLibs=false keeps its libraries uncompressed in
# split_config.arm64_v8a.apk and `lib/arm64` stays empty. System.loadLibrary copes (the zip path comes from the linker
# namespace), but SoLoader, which React Native loads its libraries with, builds its own paths from the device's first
# ABI: `<apk>!/lib/x86_64`, for every apk including the ARM one, and finds nothing:
#   SoLoaderDSONotFoundError: couldn't find DSO to load: libreactnative.so ... Native lib dir: .../lib/arm64
# Extracted libraries are found by SoLoader's ApplicationSoSource in the native library directory. Tesla (rank 96),
# Revanced (rank 151), 03-04.11.2026; checked first by hand: libraries unzipped into lib/arm64, the app runs.
#
# Applies to every app, also x86_64 ones, for simplicity: the price is disk space, the libraries are stored twice. The
# branch for apps on the system image is kept, /system is read-only.
#
# Two places read the flag, both are needed: shouldExtractLibs decides between copying and only finding the ABI, and
# createNativeLibraryHandle hands it to NativeLibraryHelper.Handle, whose native copy skips uncompressed libraries when
# it is false (with the first place alone nothing is copied).
#
# NOT BUILT (no build machine). Applied in binary form to classes2.dex of services.jar:
#   bin/dexpatch.sh DropCheckPatch in.dex out.dex 'Lcom/android/server/pm/PackageAbiHelperImpl;' shouldExtractLibs \
#       isExtractNativeLibrariesRequested
#   bin/dexpatch.sh ForceCallResultPatch in.dex out.dex 'Lcom/android/server/pm/parsing/pkg/AndroidPackageUtils;' \
#       createNativeLibraryHandle isExtractNativeLibrariesRequested 1
# then the jar is repacked with the dex stored and 4-byte aligned, and oat/x86_64/services.{odex,vdex,art} are removed
# from the image. Without them system_server runs services from dex: the boot time did not change noticeably here.
#
# Regression on probe 7, 04.11.2026: WhatsApp, Stickman Hook unchanged. Instagram 454 finishes itself on the first start
# (WaitingForStringsActivity, "InstagramMainActivity is not the root"), the second start opens; not compared with an
# image without 0035 on this version.
#
# Below: android17-release, the code as read back from the bytecode.
--- a/services/core/java/com/android/server/pm/PackageAbiHelperImpl.java
+++ b/services/core/java/com/android/server/pm/PackageAbiHelperImpl.java
@@
     private boolean shouldExtractLibs(AndroidPackage pkg, boolean isSystemApp,
             boolean isUpdatedSystemApp) {
-        boolean extractLibs = !AndroidPackageUtils.isLibrary(pkg)
-                && pkg.isExtractNativeLibrariesRequested();
+        // WSA: SoLoader cannot read an ARM library from an apk on an x86_64 device. docs/patches/0035.
+        boolean extractLibs = !AndroidPackageUtils.isLibrary(pkg);
         if (isSystemApp && !isUpdatedSystemApp) {
             return false;
         }
         return extractLibs;
     }
--- a/services/core/java/com/android/server/pm/parsing/pkg/AndroidPackageUtils.java
+++ b/services/core/java/com/android/server/pm/parsing/pkg/AndroidPackageUtils.java
@@
         return NativeLibraryHelper.Handle.create(
                 AndroidPackageUtils.getAllCodePaths(pkg),
                 pkg.isMultiArch(),
-                pkg.isExtractNativeLibrariesRequested(),
+                true /* WSA: docs/patches/0035 */,
                 pkg.isDebuggable(),
                 isPageSizeAppCompatEnabled);
